**The single most important thing, verified:** `GET /cms-akira-shell/login` was **not** declared. A fresh anonymous visit still reaches the kernel login form. `/forbidden` was also left undeclared and still returns its own 403, not a dispatch denial.

**Why 7 of the 8 table entries are excluded:** the dispatch guard's `authorize()` is fail-closed, while the in-handler `call()` is fail-open. Only `akira.post.admin.get@1` and `akira.post.admin.list@1` have tenant policy rows; every other read the declare table points at is deliberately ungoverned until increment R5. Declaring any of them would have produced a 403 for every operator, exactly the regression the contract warns about. That is confirmed in code, in the tenant 54 policy table, and by test assertion, and the excluded pages were loaded in a real browser to prove the exclusions did not break them.
